{"id":"pr-1470-draft-upbqdn-legacy-tree-roots","number":null,"title":"Note Commitment Tree Roots for the Legacy P2P Protocol","status":"Draft","statusDetail":null,"category":"Network","owners":["Marek"],"created":"2026-11-18","license":"MIT","discussionsTo":"https://github.com/ZcashFoundation/zebra/pull/12427","pullRequest":null,"kind":"proposal","format":"rst","source":"https://github.com/zcash/zips/blob/610f809954372b32a6858f410210715343ec2e3a/zips/draft-upbqdn-legacy-tree-roots.rst","official":"https://github.com/zcash/zips/pull/1470","updatedAt":"2026-11-18T17:28:22Z","summary":"This ZIP adds a service bit and two messages, gettreeroots and treeroots, to the legacy protocol. With them a node obtains the tree roots of a range of blocks from a peer. The node does not trust the peer: it checks each block's roots…","words":1342,"digest":"96771bdcb0c192fca243be39e0e32a0c92ee917cb3e76c98bbe9293dc61ba623","headings":[{"id":"terminology","title":"Terminology","level":2},{"id":"abstract","title":"Abstract","level":2},{"id":"motivation","title":"Motivation","level":2},{"id":"privacy-implications","title":"Privacy Implications","level":2},{"id":"non-requirements","title":"Non-requirements","level":2},{"id":"specification","title":"Specification","level":2},{"id":"service-bit","title":"Service bit","level":3},{"id":"gettreeroots","title":"gettreeroots","level":3},{"id":"treeroots","title":"treeroots","level":3},{"id":"answering-requests","title":"Answering requests","level":3},{"id":"sending-requests","title":"Sending requests","level":3},{"id":"verifying-roots","title":"Verifying roots","level":3},{"id":"rationale","title":"Rationale","level":2},{"id":"security-considerations","title":"Security Considerations","level":2},{"id":"deployment","title":"Deployment","level":2},{"id":"test-vectors","title":"Test Vectors","level":2},{"id":"reference-implementation","title":"Reference implementation","level":2},{"id":"references","title":"References","level":2}],"body":[{"tag":"h2","children":["Terminology"],"id":"terminology"},{"tag":"p","children":["The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"SHOULD\", and \"MAY\" in this document are to be interpreted as described in BCP 14 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["1"],"href":"#bcp14","id":"footnote-reference-1"}]}," when, and only when, they appear in all capitals."]},{"tag":"p","children":["The term \"network upgrade\" in this document is to be interpreted as described in ZIP 200. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["2"],"href":"#zip-0200","id":"footnote-reference-2"}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["\"Legacy protocol\" means the P2P network protocol specified in ZIP 204. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["3"],"href":"#zip-0204","id":"footnote-reference-3"}]}," ","uint8",", ","uint32",", and CompactSize are as defined there."]},{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"em","children":["tree roots"]}," of a block are its Sapling, Orchard, and Ironwood note commitment tree roots, that is, the roots of those trees after the block's note commitments are appended. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["8"],"href":"#protocol","id":"footnote-reference-4"}]}," ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["5"],"href":"#zip-0229","id":"footnote-reference-5"}]}]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Abstract"],"id":"abstract"},{"tag":"p","children":["This ZIP adds a service bit and two messages, ","gettreeroots"," and ","treeroots",", to the legacy protocol. With them a node obtains the tree roots of a range of blocks from a peer. The node does not trust the peer: it checks each block's roots against the commitments in the headers of that block and its successor. A node syncing from checkpoints can then maintain its chain history tree without computing the Sapling, Orchard, and Ironwood note commitment trees."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Motivation"],"id":"motivation"},{"tag":"p","children":["A node needs every block's tree roots. They are committed to by the chain history tree ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["4"],"href":"#zip-0221","id":"footnote-reference-6"}]},", and are the anchors that later spends reference. Computing them requires updating the note commitment trees, which is most of the cost of committing blocks with many shielded outputs. During checkpoint sync, the node needs the trees only for their roots."]},{"tag":"p","children":["The roots are small and are authenticated by block headers, so any peer can supply them. The draft version 2 P2P protocol has a ","get-tree-roots"," request for this purpose. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["11"],"href":"#p2p-v2","id":"footnote-reference-7"}]}," This ZIP specifies the equivalent for the legacy protocol."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Privacy Implications"],"id":"privacy-implications"},{"tag":"p","children":["Requests reveal the heights a node is syncing, as ","getheaders"," and ","getdata"," already do."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Non-requirements"],"id":"non-requirements"},{"tag":"p","children":["This ZIP does not provide note commitment tree frontiers, Sprout roots, or historical tree states. A node that uses supplied roots instead of updating its trees cannot update them again until it obtains authenticated frontiers by other means, which this ZIP does not specify."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Specification"],"id":"specification"},{"tag":"h3","children":["Service bit"],"id":"service-bit"},{"tag":"p","children":["NODE_TREE_ROOTS"," (bit 3) in the ","services"," field of a ","version"," message signals that the node answers ","gettreeroots",". A node MUST NOT send ","gettreeroots"," to a peer that did not set this bit in its ","version"," message."]},{"tag":"h3","children":["gettreeroots"],"id":"gettreeroots"},{"tag":"dl","children":[{"tag":"dt","children":["Command",":"]},{"tag":"dd","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["gettreeroots"]}]},{"tag":"dt","children":["Direction",":"]},{"tag":"dd","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["Both"]}]},{"tag":"dt","children":["Payload",":"]},{"tag":"dd","children":[{"tag":"table","children":[{"tag":"thead","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["Size"]}]},{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["Field"]}]},{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["Description"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["4"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["start_height"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["Height of the first block (","uint32",")."]}]}]},{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["32"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["final_hash"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["Hash of the last block in the range."]}]}]},{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["4"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["count"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["Number of blocks, from 1 to 4000 (","uint32",")."]}]}]}]}]}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["Requests the tree roots of the blocks at heights ","start_height"," to ","end",", where ","end = start_height + count - 1",", computed without wrapping. ","final_hash"," is in the internal byte order used for ","hashPrevBlock",". ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["10"],"href":"#protocol-blockheader","id":"footnote-reference-8"}]}," A node MUST reject a ","gettreeroots"," message whose ","count"," is 0 or greater than 4000."]},{"tag":"h3","children":["treeroots"],"id":"treeroots"},{"tag":"dl","children":[{"tag":"dt","children":["Command",":"]},{"tag":"dd","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["treeroots"]}]},{"tag":"dt","children":["Direction",":"]},{"tag":"dd","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["Both"]}]},{"tag":"dt","children":["Payload",":"]},{"tag":"dd","children":[{"tag":"table","children":[{"tag":"thead","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["Size"]}]},{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["Field"]}]},{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["Description"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["1"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["result"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["0 for roots, 1 for a refusal (","uint8",")."]}]}]},{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["varies"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["n"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["Number of entries, present only if ","result"," is 0 (CompactSize)."]}]}]},{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["varies"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["entries"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["n"," entries, present only if ","result"," is 0."]}]}]}]}]}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["Each entry has the following format:"]},{"tag":"blockquote","children":[{"tag":"table","children":[{"tag":"thead","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["Size"]}]},{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["Field"]}]},{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["Description"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["32"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["sapling_root"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["Sapling note commitment tree root."]}]}]},{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["32"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["orchard_root"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["Orchard note commitment tree root."]}]}]},{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["32"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["ironwood_root"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["Ironwood note commitment tree root."]}]}]},{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["1"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["has_auth_data_root"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["0 or 1 (","uint8",")."]}]}]},{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["0 or 32"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["auth_data_root"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["Authorizing data root of the next block, present only if ","has_auth_data_root"," is 1."]}]}]}]}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["sapling_root",", ","orchard_root",", and ","ironwood_root"," are encoded as ","anchorSapling",", ","anchorOrchard",", and ","anchorIronwood"," respectively. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["9"],"href":"#protocol-txnencoding","id":"footnote-reference-9"}]}," ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["5"],"href":"#zip-0229","id":"footnote-reference-10"}]}," ","auth_data_root"," is a ","hashAuthDataRoot"," value as defined in ZIP 244. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["6"],"href":"#zip-0244","id":"footnote-reference-11"}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["A node MUST reject a ","treeroots"," message whose ","result"," or ","has_auth_data_root"," is neither 0 nor 1, whose ","n"," is greater than 4000, or that contains a non-canonical root encoding."]},{"tag":"h3","children":["Answering requests"],"id":"answering-requests"},{"tag":"p","children":["A node that advertises ","NODE_TREE_ROOTS"," SHOULD answer each ","gettreeroots"," with a ","treeroots",", sending a refusal when it does not serve the request, for example because it is busy or lacks the data. It MUST NOT send more than one ","treeroots"," per ","gettreeroots",", nor a ","treeroots"," that was not requested."]},{"tag":"p","children":["A node MUST NOT send entries unless its best chain has a block at height ","end"," with hash ","final_hash",". Entry ","i",", for ","0 <= i < n"," where ","1 <= n <= count",", MUST hold the tree roots of the block at height ","start_height + i"," on that chain. ","auth_data_root"," MUST be present if and only if the next block, at height ","start_height + i + 1",", is at or after NU5 activation; it is then that block's ","hashAuthDataRoot","."]},{"tag":"p","children":["Computing ","auth_data_root"," requires the next block's authorizing data, so a node SHOULD bound the block data it reads per request, sending fewer than ","count"," entries if needed."]},{"tag":"h3","children":["Sending requests"],"id":"sending-requests"},{"tag":"p","children":["A node MUST NOT send ","gettreeroots"," on a connection while an earlier ","gettreeroots"," on that connection is unanswered. A node that stops waiting for an answer MUST NOT send another ","gettreeroots"," on that connection, since a late answer cannot be matched to its request."]},{"tag":"p","children":["A node MUST ignore a ","treeroots"," received while no ","gettreeroots"," is outstanding on that connection, MUST reject one with more than ","count"," entries, and MUST treat one with no entries as a refusal."]},{"tag":"h3","children":["Verifying roots"],"id":"verifying-roots"},{"tag":"p","children":["Before using the entry for the block ","B"," at height ","h",", a node MUST have authenticated ","B"," and the header at height ","h + 1"," on its chain, for example by checkpoint verification, and MUST check that:"]},{"tag":"ol","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["the root of each pool whose network upgrade (Sapling, NU5, or NU6.3 respectively) is not active at height ","h"," is the root of its empty tree;"]}]},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["if ","h"," is at or after Sapling activation and before Heartwood activation, ","sapling_root"," equals the ","hashFinalSaplingRoot"," field of ","B","'s header;"]}]},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["if ","h + 1"," is at or after Heartwood activation, the header at height ","h + 1"," commits to the ","hashChainHistoryRoot"," of the chain history tree after appending ","B",", computed as specified in ZIP 221 and ZIP 258 with the supplied roots as ","B","'s tree roots, or to all zero bytes if that header's block activates Heartwood. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["4"],"href":"#zip-0221","id":"footnote-reference-12"}]}," ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["7"],"href":"#zip-0258","id":"footnote-reference-13"}]}," If that header's commitment is ","hashBlockCommitments",", the node MUST compute it with ","auth_data_root"," as ","hashAuthDataRoot",", and MUST reject the entry if ","auth_data_root"," is absent. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["6"],"href":"#zip-0244","id":"footnote-reference-14"}]}]}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["A node MUST NOT use an entry that fails these checks, and MAY disconnect the peer that sent it."]},{"tag":"p","children":["auth_data_root"," does not authenticate the next block's transactions. A node MUST check that block's authorizing data root against a verified ","auth_data_root","; if they differ, the block is invalid, not the entry."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Rationale"],"id":"rationale"},{"tag":"p","children":["The final block hash anchors the requested range, including when the answer is a prefix."]},{"tag":"p","children":["Refusals let a requester try another peer at once instead of waiting for a timeout."]},{"tag":"p","children":["From NU5, a header commits to the history tree of the preceding blocks together with its own block's ","hashAuthDataRoot",". ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["6"],"href":"#zip-0244","id":"footnote-reference-15"}]}," Supplying that digest lets a node verify an entry without the next block's authorizing data, and tell an invalid entry from an invalid block."]},{"tag":"p","children":["4000 entries with ","auth_data_root"," take 516,004 bytes, within ZIP 204's 2 MiB message limit."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Security Considerations"],"id":"security-considerations"},{"tag":"p","children":["The request does not anchor the successor at height ","end + 1",". A peer whose chain diverges there can supply an entry for height ","end"," that fails check 3 and be penalized."]},{"tag":"p","children":["Root authentication does not ensure availability. A node that has stopped updating its trees depends on peers serving roots until it obtains frontiers."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Deployment"],"id":"deployment"},{"tag":"p","children":["This ZIP changes no consensus rules or existing messages. Bit 3 is also proposed for this capability by the version 2 draft ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["11"],"href":"#p2p-v2","id":"footnote-reference-16"}]},"; its allocation requires agreement with that draft and the ZIP Editors."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Test Vectors"],"id":"test-vectors"},{"tag":"p","children":["Payloads only. Except for the empty-tree roots, hashes and roots are arbitrary bytes, not chain data."]},{"tag":"p","children":["A request for 2 blocks from height 100000, with ","final_hash"," bytes ","00"," to ","1f",":"]},{"tag":"pre","children":["a0860100\n000102030405060708090a0b0c0d0e0f101112131415161718191a1b1c1d1e1f\n02000000"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A refusal:"]},{"tag":"pre","children":["01"]},{"tag":"p","children":["One entry with the empty-tree roots and no ","auth_data_root"," (99 bytes):"]},{"tag":"pre","children":["00 01\nfbc2f4300c01f0b7820d00e3347c8da4ee614674376cbc45359daa54f9b5493e\nae2935f1dfd8a24aed7c70df7de3a668eb7a49b1319880dde2bbd9031ae5d82f\nae2935f1dfd8a24aed7c70df7de3a668eb7a49b1319880dde2bbd9031ae5d82f\n00"]},{"tag":"p","children":["One entry with roots of bytes ","01",", ","02",", and ","03",", and ","auth_data_root"," bytes ","04"," (131 bytes):"]},{"tag":"pre","children":["00 01\n0101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101\n0202020202020202020202020202020202020202020202020202020202020202\n0303030303030303030303030303030303030303030303030303030303030303\n01\n0404040404040404040404040404040404040404040404040404040404040404"]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Reference implementation"],"id":"reference-implementation"},{"tag":"p","children":["Zebra PR #12427, commit ","69b1f48e6115e94942a5b11443b9344829b053ba",". ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["12"],"href":"#zebra-12427","id":"footnote-reference-17"}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["This revision implements the wire format and root verification; connection-lifecycle conformance is incomplete."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["References"],"id":"references"},{"tag":"ol","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Information on BCP 14 — \"RFC 2119: Key words for use in RFCs to Indicate Requirement Levels\" and \"RFC 8174: Ambiguity of Uppercase vs Lowercase in RFC 2119 Key Words\""],"href":"https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/bcp14"}]}],"id":"bcp14"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["ZIP 200: Network Upgrade Mechanism"],"href":"?view=governance&section=zips&record=zip-0200"}]}],"id":"zip-0200"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["ZIP 204: Zcash P2P Network Protocol"],"href":"?view=governance&section=zips&record=zip-0204"}]}],"id":"zip-0204"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["ZIP 221: FlyClient - Consensus-Layer Changes"],"href":"?view=governance&section=zips&record=zip-0221"}]}],"id":"zip-0221"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["ZIP 229: Version 6 Transaction Format"],"href":"?view=governance&section=zips&record=zip-0229"}]}],"id":"zip-0229"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["ZIP 244: Transaction Identifier Non-Malleability"],"href":"?view=governance&section=zips&record=zip-0244"}]}],"id":"zip-0244"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["ZIP 258: Deployment of the NU6.3 Network Upgrade"],"href":"?view=governance&s